Speech for Folio (test build)
=============================

This plugin lets Folio read documents aloud, with a natural-sounding
English (UK) voice made with Piper.

Putting it in
  Drag the !Folio in FolioSpeech-<version>.zip over your own !Folio: that
  puts this Speech folder in !Folio.Plugins. (It can go in
  <Choices$Write>.Folio.Plugins instead, where it stays when you put in a
  newer !Folio.) Then quit Folio and run it again. A speaker button appears
  at the right of the toolbar. To take speech out, delete the folder.

Needs
  - A Raspberry Pi 2 or later (any machine with NEON).
  - About 100 MB of free memory while the voice loads (65 MB after).
  - SharedSound 1.07, StreamManager 0.03 and SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 in
    System:Modules, as for !SoftMIDI. SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager
    are freeware by John Duffell and can't be included here: get ssb.zip
    and merge its !System into yours. LoadSound (run by Folio the first
    time it reads aloud) loads them.

Using it
  Click the speaker button (or choose Read aloud from the document's menu)
  to hear the document from the top of the page you're looking at, or from
  the sentence the selection is in. The sentence being read is shown with
  a tinted band; the pages turn as it goes. Click again to stop.
  Speak selection reads just the selected text. Reading speed has Slower,
  Normal (a comfortable pace for listening) and Faster (the voice's own
  speed).
  The first time, the voice takes a few seconds to load.
  It works up to three sentences ahead of what you're hearing, then rests,
  so it doesn't take the machine's time while it waits.

If there are gaps between sentences
  Each sentence is logged ("speech: 3.20 s of speech made in 1.90 s"), in
  <Wimp$ScrapDir>.FolioLog. If the time to make one is
  longer than the speech itself, the machine can't keep up: close other
  busy tasks, or try Faster.

